      trivia: "Two accounts explain the name 'Santa Clara'. One traces it to the family farm Santa Clara that yielded their finest harvest; the other holds that it commemorated founder Jorge Ortiz's father's birthday falling on the feast day of St Clare (Santa Clara Day). The wrapper is San Andrés Capa Fina Rosada, the binder morron limpio, and the filler San Andrés leaf. The factory at San Andrés Tuxtla is today a local landmark listed in tourist guides."
